# `after` reading a parent binding: the capture fact of [LTAC.3.5]. The
# follow-up rule `$arm_after_0` has no `m` of its own: `m.zone` in its
# body is a snapshot the parent took when it fired. The compiler binds a fresh
# `ds_gensym()` per parent activation, asserts the timer with that correlation
# and a `$CaptureBindings_arm_after_0` fact carrying it plus `m.zone`, and
# the follow-up joins the capture on `corr` and reads the slot from it.
#
# Two activations, two zones: a shared correlation would log each zone twice,
# and a missing join nothing. Each follow-up retracts its own timer and
# capture, so working memory ends with the two Motions and the current tick.
schema Motion scope logical:
    zone: Int key

rule arm:
    Motion m
->
    log info "armed {m.zone}"
    after 5_min:
        log info "off {m.zone}"
